Don't you think looking for a new city to live in

277
00:14:57,710 --> 00:15:00,070
is a bit of an overreaction?

278
00:15:00,070 --> 00:15:01,930
Our apartment was broken into

279
00:15:01,930 --> 00:15:04,170
Our security system tried to kill me

280
00:15:04,170 --> 00:15:06,740
And as a result   I'm leaving Pasadena forever.

281
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:08,890
Tell me how that's overreacting.

282
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:11,670
Come on   Sheldon   you can't move.

283
00:15:11,670 --> 00:15:13,080
Don't you need to stay in one place

284
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:14,340
so the mother ship can find you

285
00:15:14,340 --> 00:15:15,840
when it returns?

286
00:15:17,330 --> 00:15:19,850
Oh   if that were only true.

287
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:23,360
Unfortunately   as I'm earthbound for the foreseeable future

288
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:25,910
I need to find a location that's more hospitable

289
00:15:25,910 --> 00:15:29,310
than the mean streets of Pasadena   like...

290
00:15:29,310 --> 00:15:31,590
Enid   Oklahoma.

291
00:15:31,590 --> 00:15:32,900
Low crime rate

292
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:35,350
and high-speed internet connectivity...

293
00:15:35,790 --> 00:15:38,110
But no model train shops.

294
00:15:40,250 --> 00:15:42,040
Sorry   Enid.

295
00:15:45,060 --> 00:15:47,160
Is he quitting his job at the university?

296
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:49,300
Oh   no   he's going to telecommute.

297
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:51,400
Everybody's really excited about it.

298
00:15:52,230 --> 00:15:54,080
All right.

299
00:15:54,080 --> 00:15:56,420
Boone   North Carolina.

300
00:15:56,420 --> 00:15:58,420
"Every summer since 1952

301
00:15:58,420 --> 00:16:01,540
Boone has hosted an outdoor amphitheater portrayal

302
00:16:01,540 --> 00:16:06,340
Of the life and times of its namesake   Dan'l Boone."

303
00:16:07,100 --> 00:16:09,860
Sounds like something that would attract the wrong crowd.

304
00:16:12,550 --> 00:16:14,550
Penny   you're from Nebraska   correct?

305
00:16:14,550 --> 00:16:16,300
Born and raised.

306
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:24,500
It will take me a few days to get settled.

307
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:27,680
After I do   I will e-mail you detailed PDFs

308
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:29,720
containing diagrams and instructions

309
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:31,540
that will guide you through packing and shipping

310
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:34,470
the rest of my possessions to Bozeman   Montana.

311
00:16:35,170 --> 00:16:37,530
In the meantime   please forward my mail.

312
00:16:38,270 --> 00:16:39,350
Any place specific

313
00:16:39,350 --> 00:16:42,200
Or just the Bozeman   Montana loony bin?

314
00:16:43,750 --> 00:16:45,370
I sense you're making a joke

315
00:16:45,370 --> 00:16:48,340
But Bozeman does have a comedy club called the loony bin

316
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:50,280
so do not forward my mail there.

317
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:52,370
Oh   come on.

318
00:16:52,370 --> 00:16:54,140
So you were the victim of a crime.

319
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:55,780
That's part of life.

320
00:16:55,780 --> 00:16:58,180
When my great-grandfather first came to this country

321
00:16:58,180 --> 00:17:00,970
he put all his hopes and dreams

322
00:17:00,970 --> 00:17:02,540
Into this little butcher shop he ran

323
00:17:02,540 --> 00:17:04,390
on the lower east side of New York.

324
00:17:04,390 --> 00:17:05,780
You know what happened?

325
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:08,510
Every customer who walked into that butcher shop

326
00:17:08,510 --> 00:17:10,460
and asked for a pound of liver

327
00:17:10,940 --> 00:17:12,650
got ripped off.

328
00:17:14,060 --> 00:17:15,220
But...

329
00:17:15,220 --> 00:17:18,320
Those people moved on   and so should you.

330
00:17:18,610 --> 00:17:20,300
I am moving on.

331
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:22,320
I'm going to be a Bozite.

332
00:17:22,650 --> 00:17:24,620
They call themselves "Bozites"?

333
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:25,730
They should. It's one of the first things

334
00:17:25,730 --> 00:17:27,680
I plan to bring up upon arrival.

335
00:17:29,270 --> 00:17:31,290
Sheldon   I can't believe I'm saying this

336
00:17:31,290 --> 00:17:33,230
But I'm going to miss you.

337
00:17:33,230 --> 00:17:35,550
Penny   as you know   I'm not comfortable

338
00:17:35,550 --> 00:17:39,120
with prolonged good-byes and maudlin displays of emotion

339
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:41,380
so I prepared a short video.

340
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:45,830
Greetings.

341
00:17:45,830 --> 00:17:49,670
As you know   I'm not comfortable with prolonged good-byes

342
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:51,690
and maudlin displays of emotion

343
00:17:51,690 --> 00:17:53,950
so I prepared this short video.

344
00:17:53,950 --> 00:17:57,160
The four of you are three of my closest friends

345
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:59,620
and one treasured acquaintance.

346
00:18:03,280 --> 00:18:05,750
Though I cannot state categorically that my life

347
00:18:05,750 --> 00:18:08,470
will be diminished by not having you in it

348
00:18:08,730 --> 00:18:11,440
I am comfortable if you choose to believe that.

349
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,500
Since you intend to remain

350
00:18:14,500 --> 00:18:17,420
in this lawless metropolitan area

351
00:18:17,420 --> 00:18:20,030
statistics suggest that you will succumb to tragic

352
00:18:20,030 --> 00:18:22,460
and gruesome ends before we meet again.

353
00:18:22,460 --> 00:18:24,350
Live long and prosper.

354
00:18:27,150 --> 00:18:29,080
Sheldon   that's so...

355
00:18:32,070 --> 00:18:34,430
You might want to lock the door behind me.

356
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:36,660
This isn't Bozeman.

357
00:18:40,450 --> 00:18:42,180
How the hell do I know who's the friend

358
00:18:42,180 --> 00:18:44,280
and who's the acquaintance?

359
00:18:49,710 --> 00:18:51,930
That is a bracing cold

360
00:18:51,930 --> 00:18:53,860
An invigorating cold.

361
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:55,660
Lord   is it cold!

362
00:18:57,710 --> 00:18:59,520
Help you with your bags   sir?

363
00:18:59,940 --> 00:19:02,530
Thank you   fellow Bozite.

364
00:19:02,530 --> 00:19:05,350
And may I say   you are the living embodiment of all

365
00:19:05,350 --> 00:19:08,800
the promises made by our lovely town's chamber of commerce.

366
00:19:13,810 --> 00:19:15,360
Wait!

367
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:17,830
Wait!

368
00:19:18,360 --> 00:19:20,190
Excuse me!

369
00:19:30,180 --> 00:19:32,990
One ticket to Pasadena   California   please.

370
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:44,650
Hey   look who's back!

371
00:19:45,340 --> 00:19:46,620
Interesting.

372
00:19:46,620 --> 00:19:49,250
The acquaintance is the first to greet me.

